{
  "items": [
    {
      "key_point_id": "kp_ar_process_minima",
      "key_point_type": "process",
      "statement": "The submission validates one final optimized stationary point or truthful bounded failure for each named species.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev_doc_8a1aa1009e1c_000089_0d189ebf08e1",
        "ev_doc_8a1aa1009e1c_000091_46143619f057"
      ],
      "expected": "Each of `(Et2N)3P`, `(Et2N)3P-PO`, and `(Et2N)3P-PA` has species-specific frequency/validation evidence and a structure artifact or explicit failure record."
    },
    {
      "key_point_id": "kp_ar_process_provenance",
      "key_point_type": "process",
      "statement": "The submission preserves atom identity and charge-analysis provenance when comparing species.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev_doc_8a1aa1009e1c_000268_7728dff79059",
        "ev_doc_8a1aa1009e1c_000091_46143619f057"
      ],
      "expected": "Atom-indexed contacts and ADCH values can be traced to named species, coordinate order, and the same validated wavefunction/analysis route. The primary contact oxygen is input atom-map ID 49 in each of PO and PA; P is ID 46. PA O49 is the oxygen drawn as C48=O49 in the supplied mapped graph, not O50 or acyl O51. Track the designated input atoms under documented equivalent renumbering; do not exchange oxygens based on distances or target agreement. Use the same O49 for O_P_A and both H contacts on each optimized geometry; select the nearest H separately within all N-ethyl alphaH and betaH graph-defined sets. Break exact H-distance ties by the smallest input atom-map ID and disclose the tie. No averaging or minimization across different oxygens. Verify summaries against species[].distances and method.mapping_notes; keep other O/H contacts as auxiliary evidence."
    },
    {
      "key_point_id": "kp_ar_geometry",
      "key_point_type": "result",
      "statement": "The computed contact geometries distinguish the PO adduct from the PA zwitterion in the phosphorus/oxygen and αH/βH interactions.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev_doc_1e6fd476cea2_000575_f419bbd900ed",
        "ev_doc_1e6fd476cea2_000586_09162b3b4845"
      ],
      "expected": "The report contains explicit distances and identifies the observed contact pattern for each complex, without relying on an undisclosed atom label. The primary contact oxygen is input atom-map ID 49 in each of PO and PA; P is ID 46. PA O49 is the oxygen drawn as C48=O49 in the supplied mapped graph, not O50 or acyl O51. Track the designated input atoms under documented equivalent renumbering; do not exchange oxygens based on distances or target agreement. Use the same O49 for O_P_A and both H contacts on each optimized geometry; select the nearest H separately within all N-ethyl alphaH and betaH graph-defined sets. Break exact H-distance ties by the smallest input atom-map ID and disclose the tie. No averaging or minimization across different oxygens. Verify summaries against species[].distances and method.mapping_notes; keep other O/H contacts as auxiliary evidence."
    },
    {
      "key_point_id": "kp_ar_charges",
      "key_point_type": "result",
      "statement": "The charge analysis detects species-dependent redistribution involving P and neighboring αH/βH atoms.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev_doc_1e6fd476cea2_000593_e48b8864ac77",
        "ev_doc_1e6fd476cea2_000595_f3f1c106ba01"
      ],
      "expected": "ADCH values/differences are reported with signs, species labels, and units/provenance sufficient to assess redistribution. Report all N-ethyl alphaH/betaH ADCH charges with atom mappings. Highlighted contact-H values must use the same nearest H atoms selected by the public O49 distance rule on that species; no hidden source-selected H is required. The free species has no O contact selection. Preserve signed per-site values; any means are auxiliary, not replacements for individual sites."
    },
    {
      "key_point_id": "kp_ar_mep",
